WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.781
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.081 --> 00:00:08.653
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.953 --> 00:00:17.179
Unit eleven: Writing Task 1: Describing Trends. Today you will describe changes in a line graph with accurate trend language.

4
00:00:17.479 --> 00:00:19.887
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:24.124
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.031
Increase.

7
00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:28.865
Increase means to go up.

8
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.194
Sales increased sharply.

9
00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:34.424
Your turn. Say: Increase.

10
00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:38.361
Increase.

11
00:00:39.117 --> 00:00:40.222
Decrease.

12
00:00:41.217 --> 00:00:42.961
Decrease means to go down.

13
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.155
Prices decreased slightly.

14
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.182
Your turn. Say: Decrease.

15
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:52.174
Decrease.

16
00:00:52.917 --> 00:00:53.778
Fluctuate.

17
00:00:54.783 --> 00:00:56.760
Fluctuate means to go up and down.

18
00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.257
Sales fluctuated all year.

19
00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:02.433
Your turn. Say: Fluctuate.

20
00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:06.163
Fluctuate.

21
00:01:06.917 --> 00:01:08.162
Remain stable.

22
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.614
Remain stable means to stay at the same level.

23
00:01:12.217 --> 00:01:13.705
The rate remained stable.

24
00:01:14.317 --> 00:01:17.004
Your turn. Say: Remain stable.

25
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:21.274
Remain stable.

26
00:01:22.017 --> 00:01:22.716
Peak.

27
00:01:23.717 --> 00:01:25.391
Peak means the highest point.

28
00:01:25.983 --> 00:01:27.484
The peak was in July.

29
00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:30.747
Your turn. Say: Peak.

30
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:34.230
Peak.

31
00:01:34.983 --> 00:01:35.926
Sharply.

32
00:01:36.917 --> 00:01:38.765
Sharply means very quickly.

33
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:40.827
Rates rose sharply.

34
00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:43.825
Your turn. Say: Sharply.

35
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:47.575
Sharply.

36
00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:49.306
Gradually.

37
00:01:50.317 --> 00:01:52.606
Gradually means slowly and steadily.

38
00:01:53.217 --> 00:01:54.845
Numbers fell gradually.

39
00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:58.276
Your turn. Say: Gradually.

40
00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.042
Gradually.

41
00:02:02.783 --> 00:02:03.610
Period.

42
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:06.477
Period means a length of time.

43
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:08.665
Over the period shown.

44
00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.450
Your turn. Say: Period.

45
00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.104
Period.

46
00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.760
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.617 --> 00:02:24.172
Visal, what is Writing Task 1 in Academic IELTS?

48
00:02:25.283 --> 00:02:35.424
You describe a chart, graph, table or diagram in at least 150 words in about twenty minutes. You report the data and do not give your opinion.

49
00:02:36.517 --> 00:02:38.365
How do I describe a line graph?

50
00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:51.437
Use trend verbs and adverbs. For example, sales rose sharply from 2010 to 2015, then fluctuated before falling gradually.

51
00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:54.027
What should I include?

52
00:02:55.117 --> 00:03:06.453
An introduction that paraphrases the title, an overview of the main trends, and details with numbers. Always use the correct tense for the dates shown.

53
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.692
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:14.744
Grammar focus: Strategy: verb plus adverb plus data.

55
00:03:15.044 --> 00:03:16.207
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:22.446
Sales rose sharply from 20 to 60 units between 2010 and 2015.

57
00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:26.580
The rate remained stable at 10 percent over the period.

58
00:03:27.533 --> 00:03:34.644
Use a trend verb, an adverb and exact data. Use the past tense for past dates, and never write your opinion in Task 1.

59
00:03:35.383 --> 00:03:38.988
Be careful! Don't say: I give my opinion about the graph.

60
00:03:40.933 --> 00:03:43.014
Say: I only report the data.

61
00:03:43.314 --> 00:03:45.151
No opinions in Task 1.

62
00:03:45.967 --> 00:03:48.642
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:49.433 --> 00:03:51.085
A Line Graph Report.

64
00:03:51.385 --> 00:03:55.776
The graph shows sales of bicycles from 2010 to 2020.

65
00:03:56.767 --> 00:04:01.576
Sales rose sharply until 2014 and reached a peak of 80 units.

66
00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:05.182
After that, they fluctuated for three years.

67
00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:10.999
From 2018, sales decreased gradually and fell to 50 units.

68
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.358
Overall, the trend was upward at first and downward later.

69
00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:20.457
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:21.317 --> 00:04:23.723
Task 1 needs at least blank words.

71
00:04:24.023 --> 00:04:29.534
A, 250. B, 100. C, 150.

72
00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:36.052
The answer is C: 150.

73
00:04:37.217 --> 00:04:39.089
To go up and down is to blank.

74
00:04:39.389 --> 00:04:42.868
A, fluctuate. B, peak. C, remain.

75
00:04:46.433 --> 00:04:48.595
The answer is A: fluctuate.

76
00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:52.980
The correct tense for 2010 data is blank.

77
00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:57.677
A, present continuous. B, past. C, future.

78
00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:03.349
The answer is B: past.

79
00:05:04.483 --> 00:05:06.599
In Task 1 you should not give blank.

80
00:05:06.899 --> 00:05:10.622
A, numbers. B, an overview. C, opinions.

81
00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:16.805
The answer is C: opinions.

82
00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.822
When did sales reach the peak?

83
00:05:20.122 --> 00:05:25.598
A, 2014. B, 2010. C, 2020.

84
00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:31.957
The answer is A: 2014.

85
00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:36.307
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.649
Describe how you write about a line graph.

87
00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:49.892
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:50.192 --> 00:06:06.849
I begin by paraphrasing the title and then write an overview of the main trends. After that I describe the details with trend verbs, adverbs and exact figures. I use the past tense for past dates and I do not give my opinion.

89
00:06:07.149 --> 00:06:08.777
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:09.683 --> 00:06:15.575
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: verb plus adverb plus data.

91
00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:21.163
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

92
00:06:21.463 --> 00:06:24.045
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

93
00:06:24.345 --> 00:06:27.509
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

